Objectives & Requirements

Project Title

Student Performance Analyzer

Objective

To develop a Python-based program that stores and analyzes student academic performance using marks from three subjects: M1, M2, and M3.

Objectives

• Add student records.
• Calculate total marks.
• Calculate average marks.
• Assign grades automatically.
• Determine PASS or FAIL.
• Display all student records.
• Find the topper.
• Search for a student by name.
• Calculate class statistics.
• Calculate pass percentage.
• Provide a simple menu-driven interface.

Functional Requirements

1. Add Student

The user enters:

• Student name
• M1 marks
• M2 marks
• M3 marks

The program calculates and stores the student’s total, average, grade, and result.

2. Grade System

Average    Grade

90 or above A+   
80–89.99   A    
70–79.99   B    
60–69.99   C
50–59.99   D
Below 50   F    

3. Pass/Fail Rule

A student is marked PASS only if M1, M2, and M3 are all at least 40 marks.

Otherwise, the student is marked FAIL.

4. Display Students

The program displays:

• Name
• M1
• M2
• M3
• Total
• Average
• Grade
• Result

5. Find Topper

The program finds the student with the highest average marks.

6. Search Student

The program allows the user to search for a student by name.

7. Class Statistics

The program calculates:

• Total students
• Passed students
• Failed students
• Class average
• Pass percentage

8. Exit

The user can exit the program using the Exit option.

Technical Requirements

• Language: Python
• Data structures: List and Dictionary
• Programming concepts: Functions, loops, conditions, input/output
• Interface: Command-line menu
• No external libraries are required.

Expected Outcome

The program should provide a simple way to enter, store, and analyze student academic performance. way to analyze student academic performance through a command-line interface.
